| `simulation/core/controller.ts` | `addStaticRoute()`, `setDefaultGateway()`; LPM tie-break (connected AD 0 beats static AD 1); `pickEgressInterface` no longer sends off-subnet traffic without a route |
| `simulation/core/types.ts` | Documented metric as admin distance on `RouteEntry` |
| `simulation/cli/interpreter.ts` | `ip route <net> <mask> <next-hop>` (router config); `ip default-gateway <ip>` (host config); show ip route header lists S static |
| `simulation/core/static-route.test.ts` | **new** — end-to-end PC1→PC2 via R1/R2, no-gateway failure, invalid next-hop rejection |
| `simulation/grading/lab-schema.test.ts` | Added default-gateway lines to static-route grading fixture |

### What works now

- Routers accept `ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.0.2` in global config
- Hosts accept `ip default-gateway 192.168.1.1` (modeled as 0.0.0.0/0 static, AD 1)
- PC1 can ping PC2 across two routers when reciprocal static routes + default gateways are configured
- Off-subnet ping fails cleanly without default gateway (`No route to host`)
- Static-route lab grading passes at 100%

